course: dictionary
lesson: 9438
title: Staircase and the steps it climbs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A staircase is a set of steps that goes up from one floor to another. Many staircases have a rail, so you can hold on as you climb. A spiral staircase is a special kind that goes round and round.
explain: Staircases are useful in maths too. «A staircase of 4 steps built of cubes has 1, 2, 3 and 4 cubes in its steps: 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10 cubes.» Count the cubes on each step and add them up to find the total.
explain: The word can also be a picture. «Think of a staircase: each step was won by people who pushed for it.» Here a staircase stands for progress one stage at a time, so the word «step» is the clue that each stage is a small move up.
explain: Safety matters on stairs. Hold the handrail and walk, because running on stairs is how people trip and fall. In stories, a grand staircase in a castle or a secret staircase behind a bookcase can be the place where the adventure begins.
fact: A staircase is a set of steps going up from one floor to another.
fact: Many staircases have a rail, which you hold to keep safe.
fact: A spiral staircase goes round and round.
fact: In maths, you can count the steps and the cubes on each step to find a total.
fact: «Staircase» is a noun: one staircase, two staircases.
exercise: What is a staircase? | A wide door between two rooms | A flat path across a field | *A set of steps going up from one floor to another | A long, narrow window
exercise: «A staircase of 4 steps built of cubes has 1, 2, 3 and 4 cubes in its steps.» How many cubes are there altogether? | 12 | 7 | *10 | 4
exercise: Which is the safe way to use a staircase? | Climb with your eyes shut | Run up two steps at a time | Jump down the last few steps | *Hold the handrail and walk carefully
test:
What does a spiral staircase do? | *Goes round and round | Goes straight up to the roof | Stays flat on one floor | Goes under the ground into a cellar
In «Think of a staircase: each step was won by people who pushed for it», which word shows the idea of going up one stage at a time? | *step | people | pushed | think
exam:
Ben runs down the stairs, and his mum says to hold the rail. What is the sensible thing for Ben to do? | Keep running, because stairs are quick | *Hold the rail and walk down carefully | Close his eyes and slide down | Jump over every other step
